<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/people-who-have-been-living-with-type-1-diabetes-for-many-years-and-are-becoming-increasingly-frail> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "People who have been living with type 1 diabetes for many years and are becoming increasingly frail" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People who have been living with type 1 diabetes for many years and are becoming increasingly frail" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "people-who-have-been-living-with-type-1-diabetes-for-many-years-and-are-becoming-increasingly-frail" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Referral" ;
    dmo:statement "People who have been living with type 1 diabetes for many years and are becoming increasingly frail, (particularly if admission is related to struggles with diabetes management at home). Discharge will often require difficult decisions and may require a specific care plan. For more information see reference (7). This group is also likely to benefit substantially from the input of the hospital social services team and early referral is recommended (8)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People who have been living with type 1 diabetes for many years and are becoming increasingly frail, (particularly if admission is related to struggles with diabetes management at home). Discharge will often require difficult decisions and may require a specific care plan. For more information see reference (7). This group is also likely to benefit substantially from the input of the hospital social services team and early referral is recommended (8)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_10_discharge_planning_guideline_with_qr_code_march_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/people-with-complex-ongoing-health-and-social-care-needs-who-are-from-residential-homes-community-hospitals-or-are-being-discharged-home-with-a-package-of-care> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "People with complex ongoing health and social care needs who are from residential homes, community hospitals or are being discharged home with a package of care" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with complex ongoing health and social care needs" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "people-with-complex-ongoing-health-and-social-care-needs-who-are-from-residential-homes-community-hospitals-or-are-being-discharged-home-with-a-package-of-care" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Referral" ;
    dmo:statement "People with complex ongoing health and social care needs who are from residential homes, community hospitals or are being discharged home with a package of care e.g. those with moderate to severe frailty (see Appendices 3 and 4 for a frailty scale and inpatient pathway), people with high comorbidity load or those with mental health/dementia issues, especially those who live alone. Where possible the DST should provide liaison/support in the initial transition period post discharge. Consider referring to the guideline for inpatient care of the frail older adult with diabetes (7)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People with complex ongoing health and social care needs who are from residential homes, community hospitals or are being discharged home with a package of care e.g. those with moderate to severe frailty (see Appendices 3 and 4 for a frailty scale and inpatient pathway), people with high comorbidity load or those with mental health/dementia issues, especially those who live alone. Where possible the DST should provide liaison/support in the initial transition period post discharge. Consider referring to the guideline for inpatient care of the frail older adult with diabetes (7)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_10_discharge_planning_guideline_with_qr_code_march_2023> .

